# milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-emmc — `minimal` profile fragment
#
# Appended to the board's Buildroot defconfig by bsp/build.sh when
# HOMEAGENT_BSP_PROFILE=minimal. It is a fragment, not a second defconfig: kconfig's
# defconfig reader takes the LAST value it sees for a symbol, so these lines override
# the base file instead of conflicting with it. Keeping one base means both profiles
# resolve the same toolchain, kernel, and BSP surface — the only delta is stated here.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. Node's V8 is the entire cost of this image: measured on the laptop,
# 1h16m of a 1h29m clean build; on gpu1i, 28m37s of 40m (bsp/README.md). Everything we
# currently need to prove — hostapd, the eMMC-CID stable MAC, /dev/serial/by-id — is
# below Node and does not need it. This profile buys that proof for minutes instead of
# an hour, and is also the closer match to what sks-hub-gecko flashes: their board runs
# their firmware, not our Z2M.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT. Not a hub image. Flashing it onto a hub board silently removes
# Zigbee2MQTT and the broker. bsp/build.sh names its artifact `<board>-minimal_<date>`
# precisely so `flash-emmc.sh arm64` (which globs `<board>_*.zip`) can never pick it up
# by accident; select it deliberately with `flash-emmc.sh arm64-minimal`.

# Node.js — the 1h16m. Everything below is downstream of this one line.
# BR2_PACKAGE_NODEJS is not set

# Zigbee2MQTT rides in as an npm module of the package above; with NODEJS off the module
# list has nothing to install into. Cleared explicitly so the emitted .config cannot
# carry a package name that no longer resolves.
BR2_PACKAGE_NODEJS_MODULES_ADDITIONAL=""

# ICU is in the base config for one reason — Node's Intl (see its section 3 comment).
# Nothing else in this image links it, so it leaves with Node. ~87M of build tree.
# BR2_PACKAGE_ICU is not set

# mosquitto is the broker Z2M publishes to. Z2M is the only client in this image, so a
# broker here would listen to nobody.
# BR2_PACKAGE_MOSQUITTO is not set

# Drop the hub-application overlay along with the packages. bsp/overlay/z2m holds
# S70zigbee2mqtt and the mosquitto config; leaving them would ship init scripts for
# binaries that are not in the rootfs, which fails loudly at boot. bsp/overlay/common
# stays — that is the BSP surface this profile exists to prove.
BR2_ROOTFS_OVERLAY="board/milkv/milkv-duos-glibc-arm64-emmc/overlay /bsp/overlay/common"
